# Remark 6.2.1: Notation for dimension diagrams
%%%
tag := "Chapter6/Remark6.2.1"
number := false
%%%

*Remark 6.2.1.* By an object of the type $`1 \xrightarrow{} 0` we mean a map from a 1-dimensional vector space to the zero space. Similarly, an object of the type $`0 \xrightarrow{} 1` is a map from the zero space into a 1-dimensional space. The object $`1 \xrightarrow{} 1` means an isomorphism from a 1-dimensional to another 1-dimensional space. The numbers in such diagrams always mean the dimension of the attached spaces and the maps are the canonical maps (unless specified otherwise).
